= Part 1 — Limits & Continuity

+ 1.1 Evaluate $lim_(x->3) (x^2-9)/(x-3)$.
+ 1.1 Evaluate $lim_(x->0) (sqrt(x+4)-2)/x$.
+ 1.3 Evaluate $lim_(x->oo) (3x^2-5x+1)/(2x^2+7)$.
+ 1.4 Evaluate $lim_(x->0) (sin 5x)/x$.
+ 1.2 Let $f(x)=x^2$ for $x<=1$ and $f(x)=a x+1$ for $x>1$. Find $a$ so that $f$ is continuous at $x=1$, and state which theorem guarantees a root of $g(x)=x^2-x-1$ in $[1,2]$.

= Part 2 — Derivatives

+ 2.1 Use the limit definition (not rules) to find $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=1/x$.
+ 2.2 Differentiate $f(x)=(3x^2+1)(x^3-2x)$.
+ 2.3 Differentiate $f(x)=(2x+1)^5$.

= Part 4 — Integral Calculus

+ 4.1 Find $integral (4x^3-6x+5) dif x$.
+ 4.4 Find $integral 2x(x^2+1)^4 dif x$.
